MOSS-LORA
=========

This repository includes vendored third-party code:

  moss_lora/model/moss_image.py
    Source:    https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-Base/resolve/main/pipeline_moss_image.py
               (also shipped in the OpenMOSS/MOSS-Image repository)
    Revision:  1ceede80badddd6a7812069619edaa5633587192 (model repo state, 2026-10-16)
    License:   Apache-2.0 (upstream repository LICENSE)
    Changes:   documented in the file header: Apache-2.0/provenance comment,
               `import torch.utils.checkpoint`, `gradient_checkpointing` flag plus
               enable/disable methods on MOSSImageTransformer, checkpointed main-block
               loop, the transformers import moved into
               MOSSImagePipeline.from_components_pretrained so the module imports with
               only torch and diffusers, a single-cast _RMSNorm rewrite, a 16-entry
               RoPE memoization cache, and cached fp64 timestep frequencies with a
               precomputed integer-timestep sinusoid table. The last three are
               bit-identical rewrites/caches: no math, module structure, state-dict
               keys, scheduler, or pipeline behavior was modified; a unit test diffs
               the file against upstream and allows only these changes, and parity
               tests assert bit-identical outputs on CPU and CUDA.

The MOSS-Image-Base model weights, tokenizer and text encoder are distributed by
OpenMOSS-Team under the license shipped with that repository; this project neither
includes nor redistributes them. Point `model.path` at your local checkout (for
example models/MOSS-Image-Base) or a Hub id with `model.local_files_only` set
appropriately.

